From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: start a surrogate of the bitness the class is registered for

Purpose: run Windows 7's thumbnail cache server (64-bit thumbcache.dll in
a DLL surrogate) for its 64-bit explorer.
Windows behavior: a class registered with an AppID that has an empty
DllSurrogate value runs in the system's dllhost.exe; a 64-bit client of a
class registered in the 64-bit view gets the 64-bit dllhost, and the
32-bit dllhost is used for a class registered only in the 32-bit view.
Wine before: without a DllSurrogate path, a 64-bit client always started
SysWOW64\dllhost.exe ("opposite == KEY_WOW64_32KEY" is always true for a
64-bit process), even for a class found in the 64-bit view; Windows 7's
"Thumbnail Cache Out of Proc Server" ({AB8902B4-09CA-4BB6-B78D-
A8F59079A8D5}) then failed to load SysWOW64\thumbcache.dll.
Change: the surrogate is SysWOW64's only when the class was found in the
32-bit view (the case the code already handles with is_opposite);
otherwise it is the client's own system directory.
Evidence: Windows 7 SP1 x64 explorer.exe opening the Computer folder now
starts system32\dllhost.exe, which loads system32\thumbcache.dll.
Scope: 64-bit clients of out-of-process classes run in the default
surrogate; 32-bit clients are unchanged.
---
 dlls/combase/rpc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/combase/rpc.c b/dlls/combase/rpc.c
index c51b59d..d42de29 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/rpc.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/rpc.c
@@ -580,7 +580,8 @@ static HRESULT create_surrogate_server(REFCLSID rclsid, HANDLE *process)
     {
         TRACE("No value for DllSurrogate key\n");
 
-        if ((sizeof(void *) == 8 || is_wow64) && opposite == KEY_WOW64_32KEY)
+        /* the surrogate has the bitness of the view the class is registered in */
+        if (is_opposite && opposite == KEY_WOW64_32KEY)
             GetSystemWow64DirectoryW(command, MAX_PATH - ARRAY_SIZE(L"\\dllhost.exe"));
         else
             GetSystemDirectoryW(command, MAX_PATH - ARRAY_SIZE(L"\\dllhost.exe"));
